<title>USA: Jacksonville Savings completes acquisition.</title>
<headline>Jacksonville Savings completes acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>JACKSONVILLE, Ill. 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jacksonville Savings Bank said Thursday it completed the acquisition of Litchfield Community Savings S.B. It said the total cost is expected to be $1.9 million.</p>
<p>Holders of Litchfield Community Savings' parent holding company, LCS Bancorp, received $17.75 for each Litchfield Comnmunity Savings share.</p>
<p>As part of the acquisition, Litchfield Community Savings was merged into the bank and will continue to serve the Litchfield community as a branch office of Jacksonville Savings Bank.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
